WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.947
So Jordan, I know Cortona is
your favorite town in Italy.

00:00:02.947 --> 00:00:04.030
Right.

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:07.910
So, I arranged a special treat for you.

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:10.235
People of Cortona,

00:00:10.235 --> 00:00:14.610
I wish to thank you on behalf of myself,

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:18.110
and my fake Italian
friend from Long Island.

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:21.793
Now, the mayor of Cortona, please.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.220
Ah, very good

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:36.020
I now would like to move
on to the great honor

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.700
that Jordan is going to be given.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:40.857
A parking space made in his honor.

00:00:40.857 --> 00:00:43.940
(scattered applause)

00:00:55.296 --> 00:00:56.935
Jordan, please.

00:01:44.967 --> 00:01:49.967
(band plays Jordan out as crowd cheers)

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:05.310
We're going to your favorite restaurant,

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:06.143
is that right?

00:02:06.143 --> 00:02:06.976
Yes.

00:02:06.976 --> 00:02:10.102
We came here because Jordan,
pretty much explicitly said,

00:02:10.102 --> 00:02:11.777
he's a big deal in this restaurant.

00:02:11.777 --> 00:02:13.443
I'm not concerned with having a big deal,

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:14.950
I'm concerned with having a good meal.

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:15.810
It's not all about rank.

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:16.770
You have this insecurity about you,

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:18.510
that you project onto others.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.603
I don't care if I'm a
big deal, a little deal,

00:02:20.603 --> 00:02:22.850
a medium deal, a neutral deal.

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:24.770
I just want to go eat a good meal,

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:25.603
how many people do I have to know here?

00:02:25.603 --> 00:02:29.362
I don't know who you are,
I don't know who you are.

00:02:29.362 --> 00:02:32.646
(arguments overlapping) are
you on cocaine right now?

00:02:32.646 --> 00:02:34.904
(laughter)

00:02:34.904 --> 00:02:37.724
(Jordan speaking Italian)

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:41.760
Grazie! We have heard that
Jordan is a big deal here.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.214
Your picture's up on the wall!

00:02:43.214 --> 00:02:44.797
Yes, it's an honor.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:50.760
Why did you change the wine glasses?

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:53.270
Listen, just listen to
me. (audience laughter)

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:55.430
This is my place, this is my experience

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:56.770
that I'm sharing with you, okay?

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:58.210
You may love it, you may hate it.

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:00.824
But, at least you'll know
you experienced it my way.

00:03:00.824 --> 00:03:04.864
I really don't, this glass
is not balanced in the hand.

00:03:04.864 --> 00:03:06.910
See, it's like top heavy.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.200
You're scaring me.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:09.820
This wine is from a few kilometers

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:11.090
from where we sit right now.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:15.860
Just say miles. We're not metric.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:17.550
What are you smelling
when you smell this wine?

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.790
In the same way warmth
gives people comfort,

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:22.765
sometimes the chill of the
forest gives people comfort.

00:03:22.765 --> 00:03:25.480
And I feel like the smell of this wine,

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:27.023
gives me the same feeling.

00:03:30.905 --> 00:03:32.970
(laughter)

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:33.870
What do you smell?

00:03:35.806 --> 00:03:36.690
You sit there with a judging face

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.920
without commenting yourself.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.692
I smell desperation, I smell sadness,

00:03:41.692 --> 00:03:45.662
I smell a need to
construct a false identity.

00:03:45.662 --> 00:03:47.900
(laughter)

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:50.530
Tuscany, as I've mentioned,
is a region of meat.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:53.540
And the meat of this region
in particular is the tagliata.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:56.280
Tagliare is to cut, the tagliata is cut.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:57.300
It's a sliced steak...

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.820
They have a pasta al fumo
which has bacon in it,

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:02.340
which I know you like,
you're big on bacon.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.480
It's got bacon, it's in this
like, creamy tomato sauce.

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.139
Ammazzacaffe is the coffee killer. Why?

00:04:07.139 --> 00:04:09.888
Coffee keeps you up late
at night, the ammazzacaffe,

00:04:09.888 --> 00:04:14.123
the after dinner drink, puts
you to sleep after the coffee.

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:16.871
Well, I think I'm gonna sleep just fine.

00:04:16.871 --> 00:04:19.060
(audience laughter)

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:19.893
Grazie.

00:04:19.893 --> 00:04:21.493
Ah, prego, prego! Rastafarian!

00:04:23.002 --> 00:04:25.980
I have the music and
soul of an Italian person

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:28.070
when I'm here, I just
don't have the words.

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:28.903
You know what I mean?

00:04:28.903 --> 00:04:31.390
You're clearly not Italian,
I mean, look at you.

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:32.640
You know, look at the way you're dressed,

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:35.167
